Jinja is opt-in. A playbook without `jinja: true` never evaluates a `{{ … }}` token: the preamble,
the step's `summary:` frontmatter (in the table and in the section) and the step body fetched with
`--step` all keep their braces, even though the global config tier defines the very keys they name.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  fx_label: hermetic label
  fx_threshold: 7
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-verbatim/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-verbatim
title: Verbatim
summary: Non-Jinja playbook carrying Jinja tokens.
---

Preamble label {{ config.core.fx_label }}.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-verbatim/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  one: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-verbatim/one/prompt.md --
---
name: one
summary: Past {{ config.core.fx_threshold }} SP
---

Body label {{ config.core.fx_label }}.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-verbatim
booping render-playbook fx-verbatim --step one
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Preamble label {{ config.core.fx_label }}.

